config LONG_QDEC
	bool "Long QDEC — GPIO-based Quadrature Decoder"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_LONG_QDEC_ENABLED
	help
	  Quadrature decoder sensor using one GPIO interrupt pin (channel A)
	  and one GPIO input pin (channel B). Decodes at 2x resolution by
	  reading channel B on each edge of channel A.

config LONG_QDEC_AVG_TAP
	int "Number of edges averaged for RPM (sliding window)"
	default 8
	range 1 32
	depends on LONG_QDEC
	help
	  Sliding-window size N for period-method RPM. Each ISR pushes the
	  latest edge interval into an N-deep ring; RPM is computed from the
	  N-edge average, damping per-edge ISR jitter by ~N. Larger N = smoother
	  RPM but more lag at low speed (window spans N edges). At 11ppr 4x
	  there are 44 edges/rev, so N=8 spans ~0.18 rev. N=1 reproduces the
	  single-point T-method. Every valid edge is pushed regardless of
	  interval (idle is judged in fetch, not ISR) so low speed / restart
	  never starves the window.
